  "solution": {
    "text": "The primary unit of BaTi( <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></math> or <math><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></math> is <math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math> (as n = 3). Thus, it is formed by sharing of two oxygen per Si atom and results in the formation of cyclic silicate.<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/cd44664a-ace2-4d68-bc12-b1f6937e9ce5.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:2.975in;height:1.65in\" />",
